{title: 344 - I Love Your Kingdom, Lord}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #344 • ST. THOMAS • S.M.}
{lyricist: Timothy Dwight}
{composer: Aaron Williams}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 344}
{meta: tune ST. THOMAS}
{meta: meter S.M.}
{meta: category Christian Church - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]I [F/A]love thy kingdom, [Dm]Lord,
[F]the house of thine [Gm]abode,
[C/E]the [F]church our [C]blest [F]Redeemer [Dm]saved
[Am]with [Bb]his own precious [C7]blood.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]I [F/A]love thy church, [Dm]O God!
[F]Her walls before [Gm]thee [F]stand
[C/E]dear [F]as the [C]apple [F]of [Dm]thine eye,
[Am]and [Bb]graven on [F/C]thy [C7]hand.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Beyond [F/A]my highest [Dm]joy
[F]I prize her heavenly ways,
[C/E]her [F]sweet communion, solemn [Dm]vows,
[Am]her [Bb]hymns of love [F/C]and [C7]praise.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Sure [F/A]as thy truth [Dm]shall last,
[F]to Zion shall be [Gm]given
[C/E]the [F]brightest [C]glories [F]earth [Dm]can yield,
[Am]and [Bb]brighter bliss [F/C]of [C7]heaven.
{end_of_verse}
